<title>SPAIN: Bayer Spain pre-tax profit rises one pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Bayer Spain pre-tax profit rises one pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bayer Spain said on Thursday that its pre-tax benefits rose one percent in 1996 over the prior year, reaching 15.6 billion pesetas.</p>
<p>Sales were 168.41 billion pesetas, slightly beneath the prior-year level, after the sale of its Sara Lee cosmetics and sweetener line, the group said in a statement.</p>
<p>Exports exceeded 35 billion pesetas, representing 20 percent of sales.</p>
<p>Investments will continue at the same pace, Bayer said. Between 1990 and 1996, Bayer spent more than 41 million pesetas.</p>
<p>--Sharman Esarey, Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
